<Layout title="About Koursea Blog" description="Learn how Koursea Blog creates practical, source-aware Korea travel guidance for international visitors.">
  <article class="page prose"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE JOURNAL</p><h1>Practical Korea guidance, written for the moment you need it.</h1><p class="lead">Koursea Blog is the editorial companion to Koursea, a zero-login Korea travel platform built for international visitors.</p><h2>What we publish</h2><p>Our guides focus on decisions that generic destination lists often skip: which map app works for a particular journey, how to show a Korean address to a driver, what to confirm before paying, and where rules may change by venue or operator.</p><h2>How we work</h2><p>We compare official instructions, public operator information and practical traveler workflows. Prices, opening hours and policies can change, so every guide encourages readers to confirm time-sensitive details with the relevant official source. We clearly separate practical guidance from medical, legal or financial advice.</p><h2>Founder and editorial review</h2><p>Koursea Blog is founded by <a href="https://www.koursea.com/about.html#founder">HJ MUN, Koursea Founder</a>. On medical and procedure guides, “Reviewed by HJ MUN” means the article has received an editorial review for source use, clear claim boundaries and practical relevance for international travelers. It does not represent a medical diagnosis or individualized treatment advice.</p><h2>Our relationship to Koursea</h2><p>The blog explains travel problems in depth. The main <a href="https://www.koursea.com/">Koursea service</a> helps travelers discover places and use field tools such as Korean address cards and local map links.</p></article>
</Layout>
